        "texto": "See also chapter 3:29. Cutting into pieces was a punishment common to many ancient nations. It was known to the Hebrews, and was inflicted by Samuel upon Agag. See 1 Samuel 15:33. Some think that dichotomy, or sawing asunder, is the punishment here referred to. See note on Hebrew…"
